cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  To cite the research, cite the two papers, listed under preferred-citation
  and references below. To cite this repository (code and data), use its DOI.
title: >-
  Assurance Gaps in an Integrated Safety and Cybersecurity Case for an
  AI-Based Perception Component in Highly Automated Driving
abstract: >-
  Supplementary material for a WAISE 2026 workshop paper and a SAFECOMP 2026
  position paper. Builds an integrated GSN argument pattern that combines claims
  from ISO 26262, ISO 21448, ISO/SAE 21434 and ISO/PAS 8800 for an AI-based
  perception component, a structure none of the standards prescribes, and
  reports the decision points and findings the integration exposes.
